@startuml config-and-llm
!include style.iuml
title Config without restarts, and an LLM that only proposes

actor "Operator" as op
participant "web" as web
participant "api" as api
participant "LLM client" as llm <<human>>
database "Postgres\nconfig_documents" as pg
queue "Redis pub/sub\nconfig.changed" as bus
participant "processor · ingest\ndelivery · runner" as workers <<hot>>

== Edit a rule ==
op -> web : edit YAML
web -> api : POST rule preview (last 1 h)
api --> web : matched events, alerts, deliveries per channel\n(nothing is sent)
web -> api : PUT /api/v1/rules/{id}
api -> api : Pydantic + rule validation\n(422 with the field path)
api -> pg : new version
api -> bus : publish
bus -> workers : ConfigRegistry reloads in place

== Ask the LLM ==
op -> web : Propose a schema / a fix / runbook steps
web -> api : request
api -> api : redact_secrets
api -> llm : schema-constrained JSON\n(host must be in LLM_ALLOWED_HOSTS)
llm --> api : proposal
api -> api : validate with Pydantic,\nserialize YAML in Python
api --> web : proposal + diff + preview
op -> web : approve
web -> api : save → same path as "Edit a rule"
note over llm, workers
  The hot path never calls the LLM. Free-text runbooks are
  normalized once at config sync, cached by content hash,
  and approval gates cannot be removed by the model.
end note
@enduml
